  "text": "Beneath the lamps' ethereal, pale light,\nHe walked the streets, a solitary sight.\nEach step echoed on the pavement stone,\nA rhythm of night, a quiet tone.\n\nLike ghosts they passed, with faces down,\nLost in their own, unseen town.\nNo glance was cast, no word was said,\nIn urban sea, his solitude spread.\n\nAmidst the crowd, he stood apart,\nA lonely heart within the mart.\nThe city hummed, a distant sound,\nWhile he walked on, alone and bound.\n\nThe animal known for its long neck is the giraffe."
